#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gametype:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Strategy, Dice"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of possible players:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Two</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kjumpingcube; is a simple tactical game. You can play it against the "
"computer or a friend. The playing area consists of squares containing "
"points. When the game starts each square has only one point, and no owner. "
"Players move by clicking on either a vacant square or one of their own "
"squares, thus increasing the square’s point value by one. When a square’s "
"value reaches a maximum, the excess points are distributed around the "
"neighboring squares, taking over ownership of them. The winner is the player "
"who ends up owning all the squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Objective:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Take over all the squares on the game board."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kjumpingcube; loads directly into game mode, so you can start playing right "
"away."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You move by clicking on a vacant square or one you already own. If you click "
"on a vacant square, you gain ownership over it and the square’s color "
"changes to your playing color. Each time you click on a square, the value of "
"the square increases by one. If the square's value reaches a maximum, its "
"points are distributed among the square’s immediate neighbors (the points "
"<quote>jump</quote> around). If a neighboring square happens to be owned by "
"the other player, it gets taken over, together with all of its points, and "
"changes to your playing color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a square in the centre reaches five points, four of its points go to its "
"four neighbors leaving the source square with one point. It is possible for "
"a cascade of automatic moves to occur if the neighboring squares also reach "
"a maximum due to the distribution of points."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Note:"
msgstr "Nòta :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Large parts of the playing area can change hands very rapidly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The winner is the player who ends up owning all the squares on the board."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Rules, Strategies and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rules"
msgstr "Règlas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A move consists of clicking on a square that does not belong to your "
"opponent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "The move increases the points in the square by one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the start of the game, each square has one point, is painted in a neutral "
"color and has no owner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each player has a color to mark the ownership of squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking a square that has no owner, the player becomes the owner of that "
"square and it changes its color to the player's color. Simultaneously the "
"square’s value is increased by one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a square has more points than it has neighbors, one point jumps to each "
"of the neighbors, leaving only one point in the original square."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"During such a move, all the neighboring squares become owned by the player "
"who moved and so do all of their points, even if the neighbors were neutral "
"or owned by the other player before."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Neighbors are the squares above, below, left and right, but not any "
"diagonally located squares. Corner squares have only two neighbors, while "
"side squares have three, and centre squares have four neighbors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a move leaves a neighbor with a maximum number of points, the move "
"continues automatically to the neighbor's neighbors and so on, in a cascade. "
"A large number of squares can change ownership during such a move."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "The winner is the player who ends up owning all the squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"&kjumpingcube;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to select colors, computer "
"player, skill level and board size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "Strategies and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try to avoid increasing a square when your opponent owns a neighboring "
"square that can reach its maximum before your square does."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try to get control of the corner squares first, then the side squares. You "
"need fewer moves to make them reach a maximum."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try not to play too close to your opponent, especially during the opening "
"moves. Drop back a square or two or pick a square on the diagonal from your "
"opponent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keep an eye out for long chains of squares that are almost at their maximum. "
"If they are yours, you must guard them against cascading moves. If they are "
"your opponent's, they can become ripe for capture by a cascading move, just "
"as soon as they extend close enough to your territory."
msgstr ""

